# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Orbit — WhatsApp messaging (Exotel)
#
# Copy the vars you need into your main .env to switch Orbit's /messages
# module from MOCK mode (every send is logged and immediately marked "sent"
# with a fake provider id — safe for dev/demos) to LIVE sends via Exotel's
# WhatsApp Messaging API.
#
# See lib/whatsapp.ts (WHATSAPP_SETUP_DOC) for the full walkthrough and the
# exact request/response JSON shapes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Selects the live provider. Only "exotel" is implemented; anything else (or
# unset) keeps Orbit in mock mode regardless of the creds below.
# WHATSAPP_PROVIDER=exotel

# Exotel API credentials (Dashboard → API Settings). NOT the same as the
# Voice Connect API's Sid/Token pair used by lib/telephony.ts — Exotel's
# newer Messaging API uses a separate api_key/api_token.
# EXOTEL_API_KEY=your-exotel-api-key
# EXOTEL_API_TOKEN=your-exotel-api-token
# EXOTEL_SID=your-exotel-account-sid

# Your WhatsApp Business sender number, approved in the Exotel WhatsApp
# console, in E.164 format.
# EXOTEL_WHATSAPP_FROM=+91XXXXXXXXXX

# (optional) Exotel is multi-region. Defaults to api.exotel.com; use
# api.in.exotel.com for the Mumbai cluster.
# EXOTEL_SUBDOMAIN=api.exotel.com

# Required for app/api/webhooks/whatsapp to do anything. Shared secret
# compared timing-safe against the `?token=` query param Exotel appends when
# it calls your status-callback URL:
#   https://<your-domain>/api/webhooks/whatsapp?token=<this value>
# Without it the webhook route returns 503 and delivery statuses never
# advance past "sent" (mock) / whatever the send call returned (live).
# WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=a-long-random-shared-secret

# ── Where to get credentials ──
# 1. Sign up / log in at https://my.exotel.com and open the WhatsApp Business
#    API console to get an approved sender number.
# 2. Dashboard → API Settings → copy the API Key + API Token + Account SID.
# 3. Register the status-callback URL above wherever Exotel's WhatsApp
#    console lets you configure it, with WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_TOKEN as ?token=.
